        "geology": "The area lies on Quaternary sediments of teh Danube river, consisting mostly sand; the present surface was reshaped in the Holocene by wind resulting in sand dune systems of well classified (i.e.) coarse sand, as well as shallow depressions.",
        "hydrology": "The depressions of the area used to be under water in springtime; some depressions harbored alkaline temporary lakes with accompanied alkaline wetlands. The groundwater table level dropped several meters after a drainage campaign in the 1970s; since then, surface water appears only in or after the wettest years.",
        "soils": "Calcareous sand soil of low humus content",
        "vegetation": "Pannonian perennial sand grassland with some shrub cover, interspersed with patches of woods."
